*Recap List*

1. How is a Database Management System useful
2. What type of database is MongoDB
3. What is Mongoose
4. What is the MERN stack
5. What is each tool used for in the MERN stack
6. Why is the Express & Node API in between the React app & the MongoDB database, why not just skip it
7. How do Express & Node.js work together
8. What is CRUD
9. 


*Recap Answers*

1. It acts as an intermediary between the user & the database, handling requests & translating them into operations

2. NoSQL -> a type of database designed to store & manage data in ways that doesn't rely on traditional relational table model used by SQL databases
   Data in MongoDB is stored as JSON-like documents

3. A library that sits on top of MongoDB's Node.js driver & abstracts some of the boilerplate code for you

4. A stack of tools not a framework, its a full stack set of tools to create full web applications (front-end & back-end)
   MongoDB + Express + React + Node.js

5. React             -> create & manage the front-end (its a library)
   Express & Node.js -> create the back-end API which we interact with from the front-end (i.e. authenticate logging in or out a user)
   MongoDB           -> NoSQL database to store application data in (user data, blogs, etc...)

6. The API layer essentially acts as a security layer, preventing anyone from accessing the data in the MongoDB database
   Express checks: is the email valid, is the password strong enough, does this email already exist?
                   without it, every single piece of data is immediately sent to MongoDB 

7. Node.js is what runs your JavaScript server
   Express is a library that makes building the server much easier
   Express is installed into the Node.js project using: ~npm install express~

8. Create Read Update & Delete

